        "code": "CONFOUNDING",
        "text": "Team offensive and defensive quality are associated with both the ability to execute a recommended mix and the probability of winning. Without random assignment, causal attribution is highly suspect."
      },
      {
        "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
        "text": "The relationship between play types, defensive coverages, and success may shift across the four seasons of data, complicating pooling and generalisability."
      },
      {
        "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
        "text": "Multiple ways to define suppression thresholds, adherence windows, and mix categories would inflate false positive risk unless corrected."
      },
      {
        "code": "BASE_RATE",
        "text": "Winning is determined by many factors beyond offensive play-type mix; the independent contribution of mix adherence is likely small, making detection difficult."
      },
      {
        "code": "LABEL_ERROR",
