      "estimand": "The association between a team's offensive adherence to a pre-specified, out-of-sample suppression-conditional recommended play-type mix and the probability of winning a playoff game, controlling for team strength and opponent quality.",
      "unit": "Game (playoff games from 2022-23 through 2025-26, all rounds).",
      "sample": "All playoff games for which a valid pre-series recommendation exists, generated solely from regular-season data preceding that series. Estimated N ~200-300 games from the 54 series.",
      "power": "For a logistic regression of win/loss on continuous adherence score, with anticipated small effect (OR 1.15–1.25), power <0.50 at alpha=0.05. A prospective power analysis would need a much larger sample than available.",
      "controls": "Team pre-series offensive rating, opponent pre-series defensive rating, home-court advantage indicator, playoff round fixed effects, game number in series, and rest-days difference.",
      "falsification": "1) Permute adherence scores within series and re-test to establish null distribution. 2) Test whether adherence to an arbitrary mix (e.g., team's modal play types) shows a similar association. 3) Test whether pre-series adherence predicts regular-season games not used for recommendation generation (should be null). 4) Check that the recommendation engine does not inadvertently use future game outcomes.",
